+# Veterinarian Free-Text Search Stays Out; Filtering the Directory Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. Like most rows, it was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, and its provenance stayed open.
+
+A 2026-09-29 request asks to narrow the veterinarian list to one Specialty. Read literally, NG-9 excludes that: narrowing a list by a value is a kind of search. The request carries the owner's decision on the row, recorded at intake:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole and decline the request.** Rejected by the owner's decision.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** This would open free-text search for veterinarians, pets, and visits. Rejected: the owner keeps veterinarian free-text search out.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text search stays excluded. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows falls outside the row.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 excludes free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute the directory already shows is not excluded. The first such filter is by Specialty, on both the directory and the machine-readable list.
+
+The owner decided the veterinarian part of the row. The pet and visit parts keep their open provenance.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The directory and the machine-readable list can be narrowed to one Specialty (`REQ-VET-001`, `REQ-VET-003`).
+- Free-text veterinarian lookup, such as matching a partial name, stays out of scope.
+- Whether filtering by veterinarian name counts as attribute filtering is left open in the PRD's Open Questions.
+- A later request widening the row again needs its own recorded owner decision and non-goal ADR.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row and preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-001) — the Specialty filter the narrowing admits.
